Session delta confirms: FIRST-LEG, 6 threads to reply to (items 1-6; 7-14 are general comments / duplicates of the same content — reply targets are the 6 review threads with PRT_ ids).

Now let me start the TDD work. Create a checkpoint? The instructions say checkpoint before exploratory work — I've done exploration inline. I'll skip the checkpoint (this is a linear task; context is manageable).

### Step 1: RED tests.

**Test A — strict-mode prologue** (in test_machineNotice.js, near the L1 suite). Uses file_read. I'll append at the end of test_machineNotice.js a new suite:

```js
// ─ gh-1392 review thread 1: the strict-mode directive prologue ─────────
suite('githubReviewFetch keeps a strict-mode directive prologue (gh-1392 review)', function() {
   test("'use strict'; precedes every statement — no helper declarations above it", function() {
       var src = file_read({ path: 'js/common/githubReviewFetch.js' });
       assert.ok(src, 'source readable');
       var idx = src.indexOf("'use strict';");
       assert.ok(idx !== -1, "the module declares 'use strict';");
       var prologue = src.substring(0, idx);
       // Strip comments: the docblock above the directive is fine; code is not.
       var code = prologue
           .replace(/\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\//g, '')
           .replace(/(^|\s)\/\/[^\n]*/g, '$1');
       assert.equal(code.indexOf('function '), -1,
           "a function declaration above 'use strict'; terminates the directive prologue — the whole module silently degrades to sloppy mode (gh-1392 review thread 1). Move the helpers below the directive + requires.");
       assert.equal(code.indexOf('require('), -1,
           'a require call above the directive has the same prologue-terminating effect');
   });
``

Hmm wait — the `(^|\s)\/\/...` regex — inside the module there might be `http://` in comments — stripped already. For the prologue (currently just comments), fine. But note: `'use strict';` itself could appear inside a string earlier... Currently the prologue has no such string. Fine. Careful with the regex escaping in GralJS — supported.

Wait, one more consideration: `file_read` global inside test_machineNotice.js — is `file_read` accessible there? In testRunner.js, loadModule'd modules get globals passed; test files themselves run with the runner's globals — file_read exists in dmtools runtime; in node_testRunner it's shimed as global.file_read. test_packRequirePath uses it the same way and runs in run_all (both runners? node_testRunner is for local node runs; dmtools runner for CI). OK.

**Test B — headless red-gate marker** (test_machineNotice.js, L1 suite area):

```js
test('the headless red-gate arm wording is a machine notice (gh-1392 thread 5)', function() {
   var mn = loadMachineNotice();
   var body = '🔴 Red pre-merge gate on the head with no armed validation — rework armed' +
       ' (gh-917: first validation included, review or no review). The rework runner pushes a' +
       ' fix and validation re-runs on the new head (validate-fresh). After 3 red arming attempts' +
       ' on the SAME head the arm is withheld and a human is escalated (no infinite retry).';
   assert.ok(mn.isMachineNoticeBody(body),
       'no MACHINE_NOTICE_MARKERS entry matches the headless red-gate wording — it leaks into the agent-facing general-comments section');
   var s = githubReviewFetchReal().buildGeneralCommentsSection([{ user: { login: 'ai-teammate' }, created_at: '2026-11-06T06:00:00Z', body: body }]);
   assert.equal(s, null, 'headless red-gate arm → notices-only PR renders null');
});
``

**Test C — single fetch** (test_nakedPrReconcile.js):

```js
test('sweep fetches prComments ONCE per applied plan (gh-1392 thread 4)', function () {
   var m = nakedMod();
   var sink = { labels: [], comments: [], logs: [] };
   var deps = nakedDeps({ 1369: ['agent:review'] }, sink, false, { 10: [{ body: consumeBody('h10') }] });
   var fetches = 0;
   var orig = deps.prComments;
   deps.prComments = function (n) { fetches++; return orig(n); };
   m.sweep([{ number: 10, labels: [], head: { ref: 'ai/gh-1369', sha: 'h10' }, body: 'closes #1369' }], deps);
   assert.equal(sink.comments.length, 1);
   assert.equal(fetches, 1,
       'the same-head dedup read and the consume-explained read must share ONE fetch per plan');
});
``

Note: consumeBody is defined inside the earlier suite — I need it in my new suite too; I'll add my test inside the existing 'consume-explained re-arm (gh-1387 L2)' suite where consumeBody is in scope. 

Also the doc-wording digest item: rewording '(gh-840 audit above)'. The existing test asserts `short.indexOf('gh-840') !== -1` — safe. But my new wording keeps 'gh-840'. Let me pick: '(gh-840 audit for this head above)'? The digest says the phrase assumes the consume comment precedes the re-arm ("above"). Change tail to: 'naked because agent:rework was consumed on this head (gh-840 audit on the same head); the next SM tick dispatches normally.' Keep concise.

Now — the smAgent wiring tests. Let me now write everything. First the RED tests, run them, confirm failures.

